{"archetypes":[{"name":"shell-state","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Bash helpers now own atomic state rewrites and KV emission under set -e, which merits focused shell-state review.","prompt_body":"Investigate the new and changed Bash state-management paths for atomicity, quoting, symlink handling, temp-file cleanup, and set -e interactions. Pay special attention to clear-stall and seed-terminal-state preserving required keys while always emitting the promised machine-readable KV on malformed input or operational failure. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"emit-boundary","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff moves Step 18 report-render decisions into a wrapper while keeping body emission and sentinels prompt-side.","prompt_body":"Review the Step 18 orchestration boundary between SKILL.md prose and step-18b-final-report.sh. Check that EMIT_BODY, WFR_RC, summary-final.md, .step17-emitted, and token-report failure handling preserve the intended single authoritative body emission behavior across success, unchanged, changed, empty, and failed render paths. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-wiring","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The change adds a harness and repins structural tests, Makefile shards, and documentation contracts that can drift subtly.","prompt_body":"Inspect the Makefile registrations, shard membership, new harness, and structural pin updates for consistency with the new helper surfaces. Verify that the tests exercise the intended failure paths and that docs, SKILL.md pins, and harness expectations remain synchronized after the extraction. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
